/* Generated by tools/gen_astro_data.py from the app's Astrology Library. */
window.NAK_DATA = {"ashwini":{"hook":"The first star of the zodiac belongs to the twin horsemen who heal the gods. Ashwini people tend to arrive fast, help first and ask questions later.","facts":[["Span","0°–13°20′ Aries (Mesha), the very start of the sidereal zodiac"],["Vimshottari lord","Ketu, so an Ashwini Moon begins life in Ketu dasha"],["Symbol","a horse's head"],["Gana","Deva"],["Rashi","Aries"]],"ideas":["Speed is both its gift and its lesson: quick starts, quick recovery, and sometimes too little patience.","Its yoni is the male horse; the buffalo stars, Hasta and Swati, are its traditional yoni opposites."]},"bharani":{"hook":"Bharani holds life at both ends: the womb that brings it in and Yama, lord of dharma, who guides it out. Few stars understand responsibility so deeply.","facts":[["Span","13°20′–26°40′ Aries (Mesha)"],["Vimshottari lord","Venus, so a Bharani Moon begins life in Venus dasha"],["Symbol","the yoni, the womb"],["Gana","Manushya"],["Rashi","Aries"]],"ideas":["Its people tend to be passionate, principled and unafraid of the hard truths others avoid.","Its yoni is the male elephant; Revati, the female elephant, is its natural yoni match."]},"krittika":{"hook":"Krittika is the Pleiades, the six mothers of the war-god Skanda, and its deity is Agni, the sacred fire. It cuts, it cooks, it purifies — and it rarely does anything halfway.","facts":[["Span","26°40′ Aries to 10° Taurus — pada 1 in Mesha, padas 2–4 in Vrishabha"],["Vimshottari lord","the Sun, so a Krittika Moon begins life in Sun dasha"],["Symbol","a razor, a blade or a flame"],["Gana","Rakshasa"],["Rashi","Aries (pada 1), Taurus (padas 2–4)"]],"ideas":["The Moon's exaltation point, 3° Taurus, falls inside Krittika's second pada.","Its gifts are clarity, courage and high standards; its shadow is a sharp tongue and a quick temper."]},"rohini":{"hook":"Of all 27 wives, the Moon loved Rohini best — and the story of that love explains why the Moon waxes and wanes. Rohini is the star of beauty, growth and devotion.","facts":[["Span","10°–23°20′ Taurus (Vrishabha)"],["Vimshottari lord","the Moon, so a Rohini Moon begins life in Moon dasha"],["Symbol","an ox cart or chariot"],["Gana","Manushya"],["Rashi","Taurus"]],"ideas":["Its gifts are charm, patience and a talent for making things grow; its shadow is possessiveness.","Its yoni is the male serpent; Mrigashira, the female serpent, gives full yoni points."]},"mrigashira":{"hook":"A deer lifts its head, catches a scent and follows it through the forest. Mrigashira is the star of searching — for knowledge, beauty, love and, finally, for what was always within.","facts":[["Span","23°20′ Taurus to 6°40′ Gemini — padas 1–2 in Vrishabha, padas 3–4 in Mithuna"],["Vimshottari lord","Mars, so a Mrigashira Moon begins life in Mars dasha"],["Symbol","a deer's head"],["Gana","Deva"],["Rashi","Taurus (padas 1–2), Gemini (padas 3–4)"]],"ideas":["Its gifts are curiosity and sensitivity; its shadow is restlessness and never feeling satisfied.","Its yoni is the female serpent; Rohini, the male serpent, gives full yoni points."]},"ardra":{"hook":"Ardra means \"moist\" — the wet earth after a storm has passed. Its deity is Rudra, the howling storm-god who is also the finest of healers. Ardra breaks things so they can grow.","facts":[["Span","6°40′–20° Gemini (Mithuna)"],["Vimshottari lord","Rahu, so an Ardra Moon begins life in Rahu dasha"],["Symbol","a teardrop, sometimes a diamond"],["Gana","Manushya"],["Rashi","Gemini"]],"ideas":["Its gifts are a probing mind and honesty about feelings; its shadow is stormy moods and harsh words.","Its yoni is the female dog; Mula, the male dog, gives full yoni points."]},"punarvasu":{"hook":"Punarvasu means \"good again\" — the light returning after a dark stretch. Its deity is Aditi, mother of the gods, and it is the birth star of Lord Rama. It is the star of second chances.","facts":[["Span","20° Gemini to 3°20′ Cancer — padas 1–3 in Mithuna, pada 4 in Karka"],["Vimshottari lord","Jupiter, so a Punarvasu Moon begins life in Jupiter dasha"],["Symbol","a quiver of arrows"],["Gana","Deva"],["Rashi","Gemini (padas 1–3), Cancer (pada 4)"]],"ideas":["Its gifts are optimism, generosity and resilience; its shadow is naivety and restlessness.","Its yoni is the female cat; Ashlesha, the male cat, gives full yoni points."]},"pushya":{"hook":"Pushya is often called the most auspicious nakshatra of all. Its deity is Brihaspati, guru of the gods, and its symbol is the cow's udder — nourishment given freely and faithfully.","facts":[["Span","3°20′–16°40′ Cancer (Karka)"],["Vimshottari lord","Saturn, so a Pushya Moon begins life in Saturn dasha"],["Symbol","a cow's udder, sometimes a flower or a circle"],["Gana","Deva"],["Rashi","Cancer"]],"ideas":["Its gifts are care, reliability and devotion; its shadow is rigidity, worry and self-sacrifice.","It is prized for beginnings and purchases, yet traditionally not chosen for wedding dates."]},"ashlesha":{"hook":"Ashlesha means \"the embrace\" — the coil of a serpent that can protect, hold or squeeze. Few stars are more misunderstood, and few carry more hidden wisdom.","facts":[["Span","16°40′–30° Cancer (Karka)"],["Vimshottari lord","Mercury, so an Ashlesha Moon begins life in Mercury dasha"],["Symbol","a coiled serpent"],["Gana","Rakshasa"],["Rashi","Cancer"]],"ideas":["Its gifts are deep perception and loyalty; its shadow is secrecy, control and holding on too tightly.","Its yoni is the male cat; Punarvasu, the female cat, gives full yoni points."]},"magha":{"hook":"Magha is the royal throne of the zodiac, the place where the Moon sits among the ancestors. Its people carry an old dignity — and a family story they are still writing.","facts":[["Span","0°–13°20′ Leo (Simha), wholly inside the sign of the Sun"],["Vimshottari lord","Ketu, so a Magha Moon begins life in Ketu dasha"],["Symbol","a royal throne, sometimes a palanquin"],["Gana","Rakshasa"],["Rashi","Leo"]],"ideas":["The gift is natural dignity; the shadow is pride, status anxiety and living by the past.","In love, Magha needs respect as much as romance; its rat yoni pairs naturally with Purva Phalguni."]},"purva_phalguni":{"hook":"Purva Phalguni is the front of the bed — the star of rest, romance and celebration. Its people know something the rest of us forget: joy is not a reward for work, it is part of the work.","facts":[["Span","13°20′–26°40′ Leo (Simha)"],["Vimshottari lord","Venus, so a Purva Phalguni Moon begins life in Venus dasha"],["Symbol","the front legs of a bed, a couch or a hammock"],["Gana","Manushya"],["Rashi","Leo"]],"ideas":["The gift is warmth, charm and creativity; the shadow is indulgence, vanity and avoiding hard conversations.","In love it is openly romantic; its rat yoni pairs naturally with Magha."]},"uttara_phalguni":{"hook":"If Purva Phalguni is the romance, Uttara Phalguni is the vow. This is the star of Aryaman, keeper of agreements — and in Tamil Nadu, the day the gods themselves get married.","facts":[["Span","26°40′ Leo to 10° Virgo — pada 1 in Leo, padas 2–4 in Virgo (Kanya)"],["Vimshottari lord","the Sun, so an Uttara Phalguni Moon begins life in Sun dasha"],["Symbol","the back legs of a bed"],["Gana","Manushya"],["Rashi","Leo (pada 1) and Virgo (padas 2–4)"]],"ideas":["The gift is reliability and generous patronage; the shadow is over-responsibility and keeping score.","In love it is marriage-minded; its cow yoni pairs naturally with Uttara Bhadrapada."]},"hasta":{"hook":"Hasta is the open hand — five small stars shaped like fingers, presided over by the golden-handed Sun of the Gayatri mantra. Its people think with their hands and love through what they make.","facts":[["Span","10°–23°20′ Virgo (Kanya)"],["Vimshottari lord","the Moon, so a Hasta Moon begins life in Moon dasha"],["Symbol","an open hand"],["Gana","Deva"],["Rashi","Virgo"]],"ideas":["The gift is skill, wit and a healing touch; the shadow is anxiety, over-control and a grasping hand.","Hasta is a \"quick\" (kshipra) nakshatra, traditionally chosen for trade, learning and fast undertakings."]},"chitra":{"hook":"Chitra is the bright jewel, the star of the celestial architect who once trimmed the Sun itself to a bearable shine. Its people are makers of beauty — and they know exactly how it should look.","facts":[["Span","23°20′ Virgo to 6°40′ Libra — padas 1–2 in Virgo (Kanya), padas 3–4 in Libra (Tula)"],["Vimshottari lord","Mars, so a Chitra Moon begins life in Mars dasha"],["Symbol","a bright jewel or pearl"],["Gana","Rakshasa"],["Rashi","Virgo (padas 1–2) and Libra (padas 3–4)"]],"ideas":["The gift is design, charisma and craftsmanship; the shadow is vanity, perfectionism and a critical eye.","In love Chitra is magnetic and particular; its tiger yoni pairs naturally with Vishakha."]},"swati":{"hook":"Swati is a young shoot swaying in the wind — bending, never snapping. Poets say the rain that falls under this star turns into pearls. Its people need freedom the way a flame needs air.","facts":[["Span","6°40′–20° Libra (Tula)"],["Vimshottari lord","Rahu, so a Swati Moon begins life in Rahu dasha"],["Symbol","a young shoot swaying in the wind, sometimes a sword or a piece of coral"],["Gana","Deva"],["Rashi","Libra"]],"ideas":["The gift is adaptability, diplomacy and a trader's instinct; the shadow is restlessness and indecision.","In love Swati needs space inside commitment; its buffalo yoni pairs naturally with Hasta."]},"vishakha":{"hook":"Vishakha is the star of the forked branch and the triumphal arch — the point where you choose a path and walk it until the gate opens. Its people are built for goals.","facts":[["Span","20° Libra to 3°20′ Scorpio — padas 1–3 in Libra (Tula), pada 4 in Scorpio (Vrishchika)"],["Vimshottari lord","Jupiter, so a Vishakha Moon begins life in Jupiter dasha"],["Symbol","a triumphal arch decorated with leaves, or a potter's wheel"],["Gana","Rakshasa"],["Rashi","Libra (padas 1–3) and Scorpio (pada 4)"]],"ideas":["The gift is ambition, focus and staying power; the shadow is tunnel vision, rivalry and restless dissatisfaction.","In love Vishakha is intense and loyal; its tiger yoni pairs naturally with Chitra."]},"anuradha":{"hook":"Anuradha is a lotus rising out of dark water — the star of Mitra, god of friendship. Its people make loyal friends in hard places and keep them for life.","facts":[["Span","3°20′–16°40′ Scorpio (Vrishchika)"],["Vimshottari lord","Saturn, so an Anuradha Moon begins life in Saturn dasha"],["Symbol","a lotus"],["Gana","Deva"],["Rashi","Scorpio"]],"ideas":["The gift is loyalty, cooperation and quiet perseverance; the shadow is possessiveness, brooding and grudges.","In love Anuradha is a devoted friend first; its deer yoni pairs naturally with Jyeshtha."]},"jyeshtha":{"hook":"Jyeshtha means \"the eldest.\" It is the star of Indra, king of the gods — and of everyone who has ever been handed responsibility too early and carried it anyway.","facts":[["Span","16°40′–30° Scorpio (Vrishchika)"],["Vimshottari lord","Mercury, so a Jyeshtha Moon begins life in Mercury dasha"],["Symbol","a circular amulet, an earring or a royal umbrella"],["Gana","Rakshasa"],["Rashi","Scorpio"]],"ideas":["The gift is courage, cleverness and protectiveness; the shadow is pride, jealousy and loneliness at the top.","In love Jyeshtha needs respect and room to be vulnerable; its deer yoni pairs naturally with Anuradha."]},"mula":{"hook":"Mula means \"root.\" It points toward the center of our galaxy and belongs to the goddess who clears away what has decayed. Its people dig for the truth — and are not afraid of what they find.","facts":[["Span","0°–13°20′ Sagittarius (Dhanu)"],["Vimshottari lord","Ketu, so a Mula Moon begins life in Ketu dasha"],["Symbol","a bunch of roots tied together; sometimes an elephant goad"],["Gana","Rakshasa"],["Rashi","Sagittarius"]],"ideas":["The gift is depth, courage and the power to start over; the shadow is bluntness, impatience and burning bridges.","In love Mula needs honesty and depth; its dog yoni pairs naturally with Ardra."]},"purva_ashadha":{"hook":"Purva Ashadha is \"the early invincible\" — the star of the sacred waters, which never fight stone and always win. Its people are persuasive, proud and very hard to defeat.","facts":[["Span","13°20′–26°40′ Sagittarius (Dhanu)"],["Vimshottari lord","Venus, so a Purva Ashadha Moon begins life in Venus dasha"],["Symbol","a winnowing fan (supa), sometimes an elephant tusk"],["Gana","Manushya"],["Rashi","Sagittarius"]],"ideas":["The gift is optimism, conviction and persuasion; the shadow is stubbornness and overconfidence.","In love it is generous and spirited; its monkey yoni pairs naturally with Shravana."]},"uttara_ashadha":{"hook":"Uttara Ashadha is \"the later invincible\" — the victory that comes after the long march, not before it. Presided over by all the universal gods at once, it is the star of principled, lasting success.","facts":[["Span","26°40′ Sagittarius to 10° Capricorn — pada 1 in Sagittarius (Dhanu), padas 2–4 in Capricorn (Makara)"],["Vimshottari lord","the Sun, so an Uttara Ashadha Moon begins life in Sun dasha"],["Symbol","an elephant tusk, or the planks of a bed"],["Gana","Manushya"],["Rashi","Sagittarius (pada 1) and Capricorn (padas 2–4)"]],"ideas":["The gift is integrity, patience and ethical leadership; the shadow is rigidity and carrying too much alone.","Its mongoose yoni is the only one with no partner among the 27 — a clue to its self-reliant nature."]},"shravana":{"hook":"Shravana is the ear — the star of listening, learning and the knowledge passed from mouth to ear for thousands of years. Presided over by Vishnu, it is also the star of Onam.","facts":[["Span","10°–23°20′ Capricorn (Makara)"],["Vimshottari lord","the Moon, so a Shravana Moon begins life in Moon dasha"],["Symbol","an ear, or three footprints in a row"],["Gana","Deva"],["Rashi","Capricorn"]],"ideas":["The gift is listening, learning and wise counsel; the shadow is sensitivity to gossip and fear of what others say.","In love Shravana needs to feel heard; its monkey yoni pairs naturally with Purva Ashadha."]},"dhanishta":{"hook":"Dhanishta is the drum of plenty — the star of rhythm, wealth and the eight elemental gods. Its people keep time for everyone around them, and life tends to dance when they are in the room.","facts":[["Span","23°20′ Capricorn to 6°40′ Aquarius — padas 1–2 in Capricorn (Makara), padas 3–4 in Aquarius (Kumbha)"],["Vimshottari lord","Mars, so a Dhanishta Moon begins life in Mars dasha"],["Symbol","a drum (mridanga), sometimes a flute"],["Gana","Rakshasa"],["Rashi","Capricorn (padas 1–2) and Aquarius (padas 3–4)"]],"ideas":["Mars, its ruler, reaches its exact point of exaltation inside Dhanishta's second pada.","The gift is energy, generosity and teamwork; the shadow is pride, restlessness and hollowness behind the show."]},"shatabhisha":{"hook":"Shatabhisha is \"the hundred healers\" — an empty circle of faint stars ruled by Varuna, keeper of cosmic law. Its people are researchers, healers and truth-tellers who need solitude to do their best work.","facts":[["Span","6°40′–20° Aquarius (Kumbha)"],["Vimshottari lord","Rahu, so a Shatabhisha Moon begins life in Rahu dasha"],["Symbol","an empty circle"],["Gana","Rakshasa"],["Rashi","Aquarius"]],"ideas":["The gift is insight, independence and healing skill; the shadow is secrecy, isolation and harsh judgment.","In love Shatabhisha needs space and honesty; its horse yoni pairs naturally with Ashwini."]},"purva_bhadrapada":{"hook":"Purva Bhadrapada is the sacred fire — the star of Aja Ekapada, the one-footed unborn, a mysterious form of Rudra. Its people burn with ideals and often live with one foot in this world and one beyond it.","facts":[["Span","20° Aquarius to 3°20′ Pisces — padas 1–3 in Aquarius (Kumbha), pada 4 in Pisces (Meena)"],["Vimshottari lord","Jupiter, so a Purva Bhadrapada Moon begins life in Jupiter dasha"],["Symbol","swords, a man with two faces, or the front legs of a cot"],["Gana","Manushya"],["Rashi","Aquarius (padas 1–3) and Pisces (pada 4)"]],"ideas":["The gift is idealism, eloquence and spiritual intensity; the shadow is extremism, anxiety and a split life.","In love it is passionate and principled; its lion yoni pairs naturally with Dhanishta."]},"uttara_bhadrapada":{"hook":"Uttara Bhadrapada is the deep calm — the star of the serpent who sleeps at the bottom of the cosmic ocean. Storms pass over the surface; its people stay still underneath, and others find shelter in that stillness.","facts":[["Span","3°20′–16°40′ Pisces (Meena)"],["Vimshottari lord","Saturn, so an Uttara Bhadrapada Moon begins life in Saturn dasha"],["Symbol","the back legs of a cot, or a serpent in the water"],["Gana","Manushya"],["Rashi","Pisces"]],"ideas":["The gift is calm, compassion and endurance; the shadow is withdrawal, inertia and hidden sadness.","In love it is steady and devoted; its cow yoni pairs naturally with Uttara Phalguni."]},"revati":{"hook":"Revati is the last of the 27 nakshatras — the star of Pushan, who guards travelers, finds what was lost and, in the Vedic wedding hymn, leads the bride by the hand to her new home.","facts":[["Span","16°40′–30° Pisces (Meena)"],["Vimshottari lord","Mercury, so a Revati Moon begins life in Mercury dasha"],["Symbol","a fish, or a drum"],["Gana","Deva"],["Rashi","Pisces"]],"ideas":["The gift is gentleness, faith and protective care; the shadow is naivety, weak boundaries and escapism.","In love Revati is tender and devoted; its elephant yoni pairs naturally with Bharani."]}};
